TDD RED captured, and it is the RIGHT red.

`npx tsc -p tests/security/tsconfig.json` EXIT 1 with exactly two diagnostics and nothing else:
  tests/security/lane-smoke.security.ts(23,25): error TS2307: Cannot find module '../fault/vitest.config.js' or its corresponding type declarations.
  tests/security/lane-smoke.security.ts(25,28): error TS2307: Cannot find module './vitest.config.js' or its corresponding type declarations.
That is the missing-config RED the plan named — not a syntax error and not an unrelated failure. The spec cannot go green until steps 3/4/5 land the real configs and scripts.

BOTH TSCONFIGS: extend ../../tsconfig.base.json (strict, NodeNext, noEmit, noUncheckedIndexedAccess, exactOptionalPropertyTypes, verbatimModuleSyntax all inherited), set composite/declaration/declarationMap false and types ["node"], include ["./**/*.ts"]. The recursive include is deliberate: `--listFiles` proves the fault project now covers all four committed Foundation .ts files (foundation-harness.ts + the three *.test.ts), which `mem:gotcha-tests-dir-typechecked-by-no-gate` records as typechecked by NO gate today. `npx tsc -p tests/fault/tsconfig.json` EXIT 0, so sweeping Foundation imports no foreign red — measured, not assumed. Foundation files were read only; nothing under tests/fault/foundation/** was edited.

SMOKE (tests/security/lane-smoke.security.ts, 219 lines) asserts only runner/config facts, against the REAL surfaces:
- imports the actual default exports of tests/fault/vitest.config.ts, tests/security/vitest.config.ts and the root vitest.config.ts — no test-side reimplementation of any of them;
- reads the real root package.json off disk (not a fixture) and pins both script strings exactly, plus the ordering property that `tsc -p` precedes `vitest run` with `&&` between them, so removing or reordering the typecheck clause goes red;
- pins the full script-key set: the 11 inherited predecessor scripts plus exactly the 2 new ones, so a predecessor script deleted by this task turns it red;
- pins each lane's root suffix, exact include list, presence of every configDefaults.exclude preset plus the opposite lane's suffixes, and the full fail-empty/serial/no-focus/no-retry/strict-unhandled set;
- pins the root config's include as ["packages/**/*.test.ts","tests/**/*.test.ts"] and that no root pattern ends in .fault.ts/.security.ts — the DoD-4 assertion;
- proves file ORDER against the production sequencer by instantiating the class the config actually pins and calling sort(): uppercase-before-lowercase (code unit, which localeCompare would invert), backslash/forward-slash normalization, and non-mutation of the caller's array.
Imports are node:fs/node:path/node:url, vitest, vitest/config, and the three configs. Zero packages/** imports, zero product authority, no security/fault PASS language.

One deliberate cast, documented in the file: TestSpecification cannot be constructed without a live Vitest project, and the sequencer contract reads exactly one field, so `spec()` supplies `moduleId` and casts once in a single helper instead of scattering casts.
